{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Microscopic Meaning of Temperature.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Microscopic Meaning of Temperature.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"microscopic meaning of temperature microscopic meaning of temperature","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Microscopic Meaning of Temperature.md","fileName":"Microscopic Meaning of Temperature.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Microscopic Meaning of Temperature","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:55\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Thermal Energy Fundamentals]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Thermal Energy Fundamentals","Fourier Heat Conduction Law","cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Microscopic Meaning of Temperature.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Microscopic Meaning of Temperature.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"microscopic meaning of temperature microscopic meaning of temperature","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Microscopic Meaning of Temperature.md","fileName":"Microscopic Meaning of Temperature.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Microscopic Meaning of Temperature","heading":"Microscopic Meaning of Temperature","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Temperature represents the energetic activity of a material's elementary particles. Adding internal energy increases translational, rotational, and vibrational motion, while removing energy reduces those modes of molecular activity.\n\nThe material state changes how that activity transports energy. Closely packed particles favor [[Fourier Heat Conduction Law|conduction]], mobile fluid particles add bulk transport, and electromagnetic radiation can carry energy without an intervening material medium.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Thermal Energy Fundamentals","Fourier Heat Conduction Law","cosmol